===CONTENT===

{#scope}
@summary: Scope boundaries and ownership model for product operations
# Scope and Ownership

This manual defines release governance, SLA policy, escalation routing, and customer updates.
Teams onboarding should start at {@onboarding} and {@release-gates}.
{/scope}

{#onboarding}
@summary: New operator onboarding sequence and competency checkpoints
# Onboarding

Week 1 covers tooling and dashboard orientation.
Week 2 includes shadowing incident command in {@incident-command}.
Week 3 requires a supervised escalation drill from {@escalation}.
{/onboarding}

{#release-gates}
@summary: Required checks before production rollout approval
# Release Gates

All production releases require:
- integration test pass
- rollback rehearsal
- communication draft from {@customer-updates}
- SLA risk review against {@sla-policy}
{/release-gates}

{#incident-command}
@summary: Incident command responsibilities and response cadence
# Incident Command

The incident commander manages prioritization, stakeholder sync, and mitigation strategy.
Escalate unresolved ownership conflicts through {@escalation}.
{/incident-command}

{#escalation}
@summary: Escalation tree for technical, operational, and leadership paths
# Escalation

Severity-based escalation:
- Sev1: VP Engineering in 15 minutes.
- Sev2: Director on-call in 30 minutes.
- Sev3: Team lead within business hours.

When customer impact is sustained, activate {@customer-updates} immediately.
{/escalation}

{#sla-policy}
@summary: SLA commitments and breach management process
# SLA Policy

Core availability target is 99.95 percent monthly.
If projected breach risk exceeds threshold, notify {@escalation} and prepare external messaging via {@customer-updates}.
{/sla-policy}

{#customer-updates}
@summary: Customer communication templates and send cadence rules
# Customer Updates

Templates must include impact statement, remediation ETA, and next update time.
For major incidents, pair this section with {@incident-command} and {@post-incident-audit}.
{/customer-updates}

{#post-incident-audit}
@summary: Audit checklist for closure quality and preventive actions
# Post Incident Audit

Verify that action items are assigned, SLA implications are recorded against {@sla-policy}, and onboarding lessons feed back into {@onboarding}.
{/post-incident-audit}
